--- body ---
## Context
Found by the cross-family seat in /gaze of PR 1517 (ticket 1149 part A), ruled Original Error by the gate: both defects are byte-identical on origin/main, outside that diff. In `skills/merge/erg-pr-merge` the close-claim fence filter (the CLAIM_BODY, SHORT_IDS and perl normalizer toggles) does not track fences as CommonMark does. (1) An unclosed fenced block hides a later `**Ticket:**` line, so a real claim is silently dropped. (2) A `~~~` line inside a backtick-fenced block toggles the filter, so a fenced Ticket line becomes a live claim and can close a ticket wrongly with no visible sign. Attribution fences become routine in PR bodies once ticket 1151 lands, hence 1151 is blocked by this.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The three toggles share one CommonMark-style fence tracker: a closing fence must use the same character as the opener and be at least as long; an unclosed fence runs to the end of the body
- [ ] Positive controls in tests/test_erg_pr_merge.sh: an unclosed attribution fence before a real Ticket line still yields the claim; a `~~~` line inside a backtick fence does not turn a fenced Ticket line into a live claim; each fails on current main
- [ ] The fence tests of ticket 1149 still pass

